  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Lamplit Tavern Stash",
    "overview": "Every screen sits inside one painted tavern. A fixed painting of the tavern interior (`bilder/bakgrund.webp`) is the page itself; a painted header with the built-in Förrådet sign and a row of painted menu buttons (`ikoner/meny/*.webp`) crown it. Everything the gang touches is made of the same few materials: dark bronze-framed panels with filigree corners, stone faces inside iron frames for anything clickable, gold metal for whatever is active, and the game's own iron item frame (`bilder/item-ram.webp`) around item cards. The palette is candlelight on dark wood: warm cream text, gold and bronze accents, near-black browns.\n\nThe Krönikan surface extends that world with one new material, burnt parchment (`bilder/pergament.webp`), held by forged iron nail heads (`bilder/spik.webp`). In the reading view the evening is nailed straight onto the tavern wall that is already the background; comic images reuse the item iron frame; story, notes and title sign are parchment with dark-brown ink. The working view stays in the incumbent panel world and stays calm.\n\nThe system is dense where it administers (stash grid, filters, tables) and generous where it remembers (the chapter wall). It is game-UI literal by intent: tooltips and frames copy the in-game window chrome of Monsters & Memories.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Raster materials carry the world: tavern background, painted header and menu, stone, item frame, parchment, nail.",
      "Cinzel for every heading, label and control; Crimson Pro for all reading text.",
      "Iron frame = clickable; gold frame = selected or active; red face = destructive.",
      "Bronze filigree corner ornaments on panels and frames.",
      "Parchment and ink are Krönikan's reading material only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Metal Means State Rule",
        "body": "Iron is resting, gold is chosen. Any selectable thing (menu, button, chip, icon picker, seller, character row, tab) switches from iron metal and iron rivets to gold metal and gold rivets when active; no other colour signals selection.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Has Its Own Ink Rule",
        "body": "On parchment, text is ink or ink-soft and the accent is wax red; player name colours are darkened toward ink (mixed 45% with #2a1a0c) because the game's tags are made for dark backgrounds. Never put cream text or gold on parchment.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Small-Caps Control Rule",
        "body": "Clickable things speak in Cinzel small caps (buttons, chips, tabs, menu labels); uppercase tracking is reserved for labels and badges that are not clicked.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Spoken Volume Rule",
        "body": "On the chapter wall, quotes are set by how loudly they were said: shouting in Cinzel 700 at 1.55rem in wax red, speaking in Cinzel 700 at 1.12rem, muttering in Crimson Pro italic at 0.98rem in ink-soft.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Silhouette Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Anything drawn with a raster border-image casts `filter: drop-shadow`, never `box-shadow`, so torn parchment and riveted iron keep their real outline.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every new clickable from the iron frame and stone face, and mark selection by switching to gold metal and gold rivets.",
      "**Do** keep the tavern background visible and fixed; place new surfaces on it rather than on a new backdrop.",
      "**Do** use Cinzel for headings, labels and controls and Crimson Pro for anything read as prose.",
      "**Do** draw parchment and frames with their 9-slice rasters and shadow them with `drop-shadow`.",
      "**Do** keep parchment text in ink, ink-soft and wax red, and darken player tag colours before using them on paper.",
      "**Do** keep controls on the shared 2.6rem height when they sit in a row.",
      "**Do** gate entrance motion behind `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce rounded, flat or pill-shaped controls; corners stay at 2 to 3px and are ornamented with rivets or filigree instead.",
      "**Don't** use office push pins, sticky-note colours or a separate board texture on the chronicle wall; pieces are held by forged nails on the tavern wall itself.",
      "**Don't** put cream text or gold accents on parchment, or parchment surfaces in the administrative views.",
      "**Don't** use cool or saturated accent colours beyond the item status set.",
      "**Don't** use unicode glyphs as icons; draw them in `Icon.tsx`.",
